``` Dashboard searches for vulntriage findings sent through HEC (sourcetype vulntriage:finding).
    Splunk extracts the JSON fields automatically; do not add `spath` (it duplicates values
    and doubles counts). Arrays appear with {} (for example mitre{}).
    Every run re-sends all findings, so each panel keeps only the latest event per finding
    (`dedup fingerprint`, then filter; Splunk returns newest first, so a finding fixed in the
    latest run drops out). Without it, counts grow with every run.
    Save each as a dashboard panel: Search -> Save As -> Dashboard Panel. ```

``` Panel 1: open findings by priority ```
sourcetype="vulntriage:finding"
| dedup fingerprint
| search open=true
| stats count by priority
| sort priority

``` Panel 2: overdue findings by owning team (SLA enforcement) ```
sourcetype="vulntriage:finding"
| dedup fingerprint
| search open=true
| eval due_epoch=strptime(due_date, "%Y-%m-%d")
| where due_epoch < now()
| stats count as overdue values(rule_id) as findings by owner
| sort - overdue

``` Panel 3: actively exploited (CISA KEV) and still open ```
sourcetype="vulntriage:finding"
| dedup fingerprint
| search open=true kev=true
| table rule_id package resource owner priority due_date epss

``` Panel 4: misconfigurations mapped to MITRE ATT&CK ```
sourcetype="vulntriage:finding"
| dedup fingerprint
| search kind=misconfiguration open=true
| rename "mitre{}" as mitre
| mvexpand mitre
| stats count by mitre
| sort - count

``` Panel 5: suppressions (accepted risk and false positives) for review ```
sourcetype="vulntriage:finding"
| dedup fingerprint
| search suppressed=true
| table rule_id resource suppression_note
